      en: ["Occupied from approximately 400 BC to 1000 AD.", "Located in the Santa Bárbara department along the Ulúa River.", "Key link between the Maya and Lenca cultural spheres.", "Renowned for ceramic finds in the polychrome Ulúa style.", "The site features over 100 identified structures.", "Served as a regional hub for the trade of obsidian and jade."],
